{number: 85}
{title: Jesus Loves Me}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] Jesus loves me, this I know,
For the Bible tells me [Bb7] so;
[Eb] Little ones to Him belong,
They are [Ab] weak, but [Eb] He is [Bb7] [Eb] strong.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Yes, [Eb] Jesus loves me!
[Ab] Yes, Jesus loves me!
[Eb] Yes, Jesus loves me!
The [Bb7] Bible tells me [Eb] so.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Eb] Jesus loves me, He who died
Heaven's gate to open [Bb7] wide;
[Eb] He will wash away my sin,
Let His [Ab] little [Eb] child come [Bb7] [Eb] in.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Eb] Jesus loves me, loves me still,
Though I'm very weak and [Bb7] ill;
[Eb] From His shining throne on high
Comes to [Ab] watch me [Eb] where I [Bb7] [Eb] lie.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[Eb] Jesus loves me, He will stay
Close beside me all the [Bb7] way:
[Eb] If I love Him, when I die
He will [Ab] take me [Eb] home on [Bb7] [Eb] high.
{end_of_verse}
